# Necro-Prune-AST-Deadcode-Incinerator 🔥

> **AST-Level Static Dead Code Analysis, Symbol Reachability Graph Traversal, and Surgical Codebase Incinerator**

[![CI](https://github.com/Sunzzx/necro-prune-ast-deadcode-incinerator/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/Sunzzx/necro-prune-ast-deadcode-incinerator)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10%2B-green.svg)](https://python.org)

---

## 1. Architectural Foundations

`necro-prune-ast-deadcode-incinerator` addresses technical debt accumulation across autonomous AI repositories. It treats codebase health as an invariant graph problem:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Python Source Code] --> B[AST Parser NodeVisitor]
    B --> C[Symbol Definition Table]
    B --> D[Symbol Reference Table]
    C --> E[Reachability Diff & Filter]
    D --> E
    E --> F[Dead Code Removing Transformer]
    F --> G[Synthesized Pruned Source]
```

## 2. CLI Usage

```bash
# Audit any project or directory for unreferenced functions and classes
necro-prune audit ~/.hermes/scripts

# Incinerate dead code in a file in-place
necro-prune incinerate target_script.py --inplace
```

